'''Jaypee Infratech Ltd''' ('''JIL''') was an Indian [[real estate]] company with its head office in [[Noida]], [[Gautam Buddha Nagar district|Gautam Buddha Nagar]], India. JIL was formed by Manoj Gaur elder son of Indian Entrepreneur [[Jaiprakash Gaur]], the owner of [[Jaypee Group]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Jaypee Infratech Limited (JPINFRATEC.NS) Company Profile & Facts - Yahoo Finance |url=https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/JPINFRATEC.NS/profile/ |access-date=2023-10-11 |website=finance.yahoo.com |language=en-US}}</ref> The company was majorly engaged in the development and construction of real estate, comprising expressways, and commercial and residential buildings. The company was maintaining and developing the [[Yamuna Expressway|Yamuna Expressway Project]],<ref>{{Cite web |last=Ghosh |first=Himadri |date=2017-10-13 |title=Insolvency: Jaypee Infra wants to sell Yamuna Expressway for Rs 2,500 crore |url=https://www.ibtimes.co.in/insolvency-jaypee-infra-wants-sell-yamuna-expressway-rs-2500-crore-745543 |access-date=2023-10-11 |website=www.ibtimes.co.in |language=en}}</ref> a 165-kilometer (km) long six-lane expressway from [[Greater Noida]] to [[Agra]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=2018-09-07 |title=Jaypee Infratech seeks ₹20 cr to enhance safety on Yamuna Eway |url=https://www.hindustantimes.com/noida/jaypee-infratech-limited-seeks-rs-20-crore-to-enhance-safety-on-yamuna-expressway/story-iuiZh2NPCzBu1H1ef0ATNJ.html |access-date=2024-03-14 |website=Hindustan Times |language=en}}</ref> Jaypee Infratech Ltd was also listed on the [[Bombay Stock Exchange]] (BSE)<ref>{{Cite web |title=Stock Share Price {{!}} Get Quote {{!}} BSE |url=https://www.bseindia.com/stock-share-price/jaypee-infratech-ltd/11jil19/951547/financials-results/ |access-date=2023-10-11 |website=www.bseindia.com}}</ref> and the [[National Stock Exchange of India|National Stock Exchange]] (NSE).<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.bseindia.com/stock-share-price/godrej-properties/godrej-properties/533150/|title=Stock Share Price godrej properties {{!}} Get Quote godrej properties {{!}} BSE|website=www.bseindia.com|access-date=2018-11-28}}</ref>

In 2023, Gaurs took over a few of Jaypee Infratech's projects.<ref name="moneycontrol.com">{{Cite web |date=2023-06-13 |title=Gaurs Group to develop 450 luxury apartments with an investment of over Rs 500 crore in Jaypee Greens |url=https://www.moneycontrol.com/news/business/real-estate/gaurs-group-to-develop-450-luxury-apartments-with-an-investment-of-over-rs-500-crore-in-jaypee-greens-10789051.html |access-date=2023-10-11 |website=Moneycontrol |language=en}}</ref>

