== Jaypee Infratech insolvency case ==
In 2007, Jaypee Infratech Limited (JIL) proposed to build 32,000<ref>{{Cite web |date=2023-05-07 |title=NCLT approves Suraksha group's bid for Jaypee Infratech; relief for more than 20,000 homebuyers |url=https://www.zeebiz.com/companies/news-nclt-approves-suraksha-groups-bid-for-jaypee-infratech-relief-for-more-than-20000-homebuyers-233714 |access-date=2023-10-11 |website=Zee Business}}</ref> housing units and plots after signing an agreement with [[Yamuna Expressway Industrial Development Authority]] (YEIDA)<ref>{{Cite web |date=2023-03-08 |title=Jaypee Infratech insolvency case: Relief for homebuyers who fought a decade-long legal battle |url=https://www.moneycontrol.com/news/business/real-estate/jaypee-infratech-insolvency-case-relief-for-homebuyers-who-fought-a-decade-long-legal-battle-10217221.html |access-date=2023-10-11 |website=Moneycontrol |language=en}}</ref> to collect tolls on the expressway for 36 years and was allotted 25,000 hectares of land in [[Noida]] and [[Greater Noida]] and near [[Dankaur]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=2021-05-25 |title=Jaypee Infratech promoter Manoj Gaur makes a settlement offer to lenders |url=https://www.cnbctv18.com/business/companies/jaypee-infratech-promoter-manoj-gaur-makes-a-settlement-offer-to-lenders-9424051.htm |access-date=2023-10-11 |website=cnbctv18.com |language=en}}</ref>

However, the projects soon became part of what is widely referred to as the [[Jaypee Infratech homebuyers fraud]], as thousands of buyers alleged that funds were mismanaged and diverted, while promised homes were not delivered. Construction stalled around 2013–2014, leaving a large number of homebuyers stranded despite having paid substantial amounts.<ref>{{Cite news |last=PTI |date=2023-03-07 |title=NCLT approves Suraksha group's bid for Jaypee Infratech; relief for more than 20,000 homebuyers |language=en-IN |work=The Hindu |url=https://www.thehindu.com/business/Industry/nclt-approves-suraksha-groups-bid-for-jaypee-infratech-relief-for-more-than-20000-homebuyers/article66591148.ece |access-date=2023-10-11 |issn=0971-751X}}</ref> Later, the Suraksha Group<ref>{{Cite web |last=Livemint |date=2023-04-11 |title=IT dept challenges NCLT order approving Suraksha Group' bid for Jaypee Infratech |url=https://www.livemint.com/news/india/it-dept-challenges-nclt-order-approving-suraksha-group-bid-for-jaypee-infratech-11681170472380.html |access-date=2023-10-11 |website=mint |language=en}}</ref> acquired these projects from Jaypee Infratech and won the case and now over 20,000 homebuyers<ref>{{Cite news |date=2023-03-07 |title=NCLT approves Suraksha Group's bid to acquire Jaypee Infratech, complete 20,000 flats in stalled projects |work=The Economic Times |url=https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/industry/services/property-/-cstruction/nclt-approves-suraksha-groups-bid-to-acquire-jaypee-infratech-complete-20000-flats-in-stalled-projects/articleshow/98474364.cms?from=mdr |access-date=2023-10-11 |issn=0013-0389}}</ref> will get their homes which they had booked over a decade ago.<ref>{{Cite news |date=2023-08-26 |title=Ray of hope for 20,000 homebuyers as work begins in Jaypee Infra's 'ghost town' in Noida |work=The Economic Times |url=https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/industry/services/property-/-cstruction/ray-of-hope-for-20k-homebuyers-as-work-begins-in-noidas-ghost-town/articleshow/103083645.cms |access-date=2023-10-11 |issn=0013-0389}}</ref>

